{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>נבוב</b> — like: נבוב לוחות (hollow boards)." "<b>ילבב</b> — he acquires heart, which is wisdom, like: קונה לב (acquires heart)." "<b>ועיר פרא</b> — like עיר (a wild ass), and פרא is man when he is born, and similar is ככבש אלוף. Rabbi Moses said: כי חלד — like חלודה (verdigris/patina) in the language of our Rabbis of blessed memory, and the meaning is that the verdigris will return and shine brighter than noon. And the correct interpretation: כי חלדך means your appointed time will arise (יקום), and the meaning of יקום is 'will stand,' like וקם הבית." "<b>תעופה</b> — some say: you will gaze. And so: התעיף עיניך בו. And others said: כי תעופה is from עיפה, and this is correct. And the meaning: if you repent — your lifetime (חלדך) will stand like the noon sun, and in the time of darkness you will return like morning, in the sense of 'he will return to the days of his youth'; you will be renewed like an eagle, תתחדש כנשר נעורייכי."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {2 "Resolved 'ר' משה' as 'Rabbi Moses' following standard identification with Ibn Ezra's teacher Moses ha-Sephardi; the citation of וקם הבית appears to reference a verse but the exact locus is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:28.534298145Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}